  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, you are required to file an income tax return if you have taxable income. The deadline for filing is typically on or before April 15 of the following year after the taxable year.\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 23 of the NIRC, all citizens and resident aliens are subject to income tax on their worldwide income. This means that if you earn income, regardless of its source, you must file a return. Section 51 specifies that the income tax return must be filed on or before April 15 of the year following the taxable year, unless extended by the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR).\n\n### Practical Meaning\nPractically, this means that if you earned income during the previous calendar year, you must prepare and submit your income tax return by April 15 of the current year. Failure to file on time may result in penalties and interest on any taxes owed. It is advisable to keep accurate records of your income and expenses throughout the year to facilitate the filing process.",
